[[0,1969243,0,2,0,2,"2017-07-01T01:24:27","IraqCombatVet","",[],"","Is the future of racing games in the past?","http://playstationenthusiast.com/article/is-the-future-of-racing-games-in-the-past/","gaming"],[1,9695344,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-01T01:57:42","o0shad0o","",[],"<p>I think VR may give it a new bump.</p>"],[1,9696082,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-01T03:18:58","BentAxel","",[],"<p>Just my opinion as this is my favorite style of game. The thing with racing sims, its either full real world physics or none at all. There is no in-between. This is the bread and butter to a racing game. On one hand you have fun Arcade games like Motorstorm and older Jet Bike that are themed for fantasy, then you have games like project cars, Grand Turismo for consoles and then iRacing for the PC. Theres two, sort of the same customer. We all like racing games, just sometimes we want to know what it really is like to race a full race livery WRC or F1 Car. Or even a low budget race car and not have to trailer it to the track. </p>\n<p>I think there is decades of making it better. Things like subtle elevation changes or track idiosyncrasies. What this means is road grime covering your vision, tire rubber getting kicked up, oil from the exhaust or mud and dirt. With tracks, someone just released the Long Beach Grand Prix course, I was watching the video of it and it was like a dream track. Ive driven that track and its filled with uneven cracks, off camber curbs, fucked up concrete slabs and actual braking bumps from heat and years of driving. So that affects the car. Suspension comes into play. Tuneability is where the next generation of games will win. On the arcade side, it will be pod racing type of things. I agree that games like WipeOut and if not wipeout, Formula 1 in <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/91/18/b2/9118b23d684a6f3a33f04af460feba1a.jpg\">2029 with concept cars</a>. Anyway, I would love to see a lot of things in games that have been discussed while gaming. Im sure because of computing power it hasnt made it and doing so would have a small audience. I feel its out there, the developers havent gone for the gap to use a racing term.</p>"],[1,9697616,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-01T07:04:49","isha","",[],"<p>good</p>"],[1,9698715,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-01T11:51:40","3dk","[e]",[],"<p>Here's a good looking <a href=\"http://store.steampowered.com/app/517710/Redout_Enhanced_Edition/\">Wipeout clone on Steam.</a> For anyone interested.</p>"]]
